WEBVTT

00:07.465 --> 00:08.508
Tanjiro.

00:11.136 --> 00:12.429
You...

00:14.389 --> 00:19.602
The Demon Slayer Corps
is not a place to play and fool around!

00:19.686 --> 00:22.397
People like you ought to be purged!

00:22.480 --> 00:24.733
I will purge you right now!

00:24.816 --> 00:28.737
Don't you mess around
with the Demon Slayer Corps!

02:16.052 --> 02:17.512
Nezuko.

02:19.889 --> 02:22.475
Nezuko.

02:30.233 --> 02:34.863
Nezuko!

02:37.323 --> 02:39.868
Zenitsu, can you please behave yourself?

02:42.036 --> 02:44.581
Tanjiro.

02:48.877 --> 02:51.880
Let's get along, Tanjiro!

02:51.963 --> 02:55.383
-Zenitsu, please stay away from us!
-Tanjiro.

02:55.466 --> 02:58.887
Don't say that, Tanjiro.

02:58.970 --> 03:00.513
Oh, Nezuko...

03:00.597 --> 03:03.349
-Stop it, Zenitsu!
-Tanjiro, Nezuko...

03:03.433 --> 03:07.687
-Tanjiro, Nezuko...
-I'm starving.

03:09.647 --> 03:11.774
Excuse me, young man.

03:17.488 --> 03:22.285
I found that your clothes
are terribly dirty.

03:23.328 --> 03:26.080
I'll wash them up
and give them back to you.

03:26.164 --> 03:29.000
In the meantime, wear this.

03:31.169 --> 03:35.173
It'll feel good and comfortable
when you wear it.

03:40.261 --> 03:43.932
Can I cook you tempura for dinner?

03:44.641 --> 03:49.354
It's the one coated with flour.

03:51.856 --> 03:54.025
Wait!

03:54.108 --> 03:57.862
Wait for me, Nezuko, Tanjiro.

04:01.616 --> 04:03.576
What is it?

04:06.287 --> 04:07.497
Wait!

04:07.580 --> 04:10.166
Wait, Inosuke!

04:11.334 --> 04:13.544
Tanjiro!

04:26.849 --> 04:28.101
You've all recovered.

04:48.579 --> 04:51.582
Northeast!

04:51.666 --> 04:54.419
Your next stop is northeast.

04:54.502 --> 04:57.213
You three are going to Mount Natagumo.

04:57.297 --> 04:59.590
Go to Mount Natagumo.

05:07.974 --> 05:09.225
We're off now.

05:10.727 --> 05:12.270
Thank you for your accommodation.

05:17.317 --> 05:19.694
Here is a flint.

05:20.236 --> 05:21.612
Thank you, ma'am.

05:28.619 --> 05:30.580
What the hell, old woman?

05:31.372 --> 05:32.749
You fool!

05:34.709 --> 05:37.587
It's a stone used to light up sparks
to chase evil spirits

05:37.670 --> 05:39.213
because we're going on a dangerous job!

05:41.507 --> 05:46.721
You should be proud of yourselves
and strive to survive at all times.

05:47.555 --> 05:49.474
Good luck in your fight.

05:56.689 --> 06:01.069
WISTERIA

06:05.573 --> 06:08.201
"Proud of ourselves"?
"Good luck in your fight"?

06:08.284 --> 06:09.702
What does that mean?

06:09.786 --> 06:11.662
What a blockhead.

06:12.997 --> 06:14.123
He has a point.

06:14.207 --> 06:16.417
It sounded quite cryptic to me.

06:17.043 --> 06:18.252
To be proud of ourselves...

06:19.087 --> 06:21.339
is to fully comprehend our own position,

06:21.422 --> 06:23.633
to be able to bear it
with a clear conscience,

06:23.716 --> 06:25.384
and to do the right thing.

06:25.468 --> 06:26.427
Something like that.

06:27.845 --> 06:31.474
Besides, the old lady wished us
a safe journey.

06:32.058 --> 06:34.143
What kind of position is that?

06:34.227 --> 06:36.604
What does clear conscience mean?

06:37.230 --> 06:38.314
Well...

06:38.397 --> 06:41.567
What is doing the right thing?

06:41.651 --> 06:44.904
Why did the old woman
have to wish us a safe journey?

06:44.987 --> 06:48.116
She's not even my relative,
so why did she do that?

06:49.325 --> 06:51.744
She didn't comprehend her position,
did she?

06:54.914 --> 06:55.873
He's getting faster.

06:56.958 --> 06:59.335
I'm not going to lose!

07:00.294 --> 07:02.713
Wait for me!

07:13.015 --> 07:14.350
Wait!

07:14.434 --> 07:15.977
Can you guys wait for me?

07:17.145 --> 07:19.439
What is it, Zenitsu?

07:19.522 --> 07:21.107
I'm scared!

07:21.190 --> 07:23.901
We're getting closer to our destination
and it's freaking me out!

07:24.819 --> 07:26.612
Why is he sitting?

07:26.696 --> 07:28.406
It's disgusting.

07:28.489 --> 07:30.992
You have no right to rebuke me,
you pig head!

07:31.075 --> 07:34.537
Can't you guys feel anything
coming out of that mountain up ahead?

07:43.713 --> 07:46.632
But still, you can't just sit here.

07:46.716 --> 07:48.634
You're disgusting indeed.

07:48.718 --> 07:51.053
I'm not disgusting, I'm normal!

07:51.137 --> 07:52.096
I'm normal.

07:52.180 --> 07:54.098
You're the weirdos!

08:01.647 --> 08:04.358
What's going on? Hey.

08:05.610 --> 08:06.903
What smell is this?

08:07.778 --> 08:09.238
Tanjiro, wait!

08:09.322 --> 08:11.657
Don't leave me alone, damn it!

08:11.741 --> 08:13.451
Don't leave me alone!

08:26.422 --> 08:29.008
Help...

08:29.926 --> 08:32.386
He's wearing a Corps uniform.
He's a demon slayer.

08:32.470 --> 08:33.679
Something must have happened.

08:35.181 --> 08:36.307
Wait!

08:36.390 --> 08:38.559
Are you all right? What happened?

08:43.731 --> 08:45.650
They're taking me away too!

08:45.733 --> 08:48.778
Help me!

09:05.127 --> 09:06.420
I have to save him.

09:09.674 --> 09:11.592
Let me go first.

09:11.676 --> 09:14.804
You may follow my lead and tremble.

09:15.513 --> 09:17.139
I'm starving.

09:18.307 --> 09:19.350
Inosuke.

09:20.601 --> 09:22.687
He can't wait to get into action, can he?

10:30.963 --> 10:32.214
What is this?

10:41.098 --> 10:42.516
A spider web.

10:45.394 --> 10:47.355
There are webs everywhere.

10:47.438 --> 10:48.981
It's getting in our way!

10:49.065 --> 10:50.024
Right.

10:51.692 --> 10:52.860
Inosuke.

10:52.943 --> 10:54.070
What?

10:54.779 --> 10:55.780
Thank you.

10:57.448 --> 10:59.742
You agreed to follow us.

10:59.825 --> 11:01.077
That makes me feel safe.

11:03.412 --> 11:06.957
The ominous warping smell
from the mountain

11:07.041 --> 11:09.460
made me a little nervous and stiff.

11:10.503 --> 11:11.504
Thank you.

11:16.050 --> 11:20.346
It'll feel good and comfortable
when you wear it.

11:20.429 --> 11:25.393
You should be proud of yourselves
and strive to survive at all times.

11:25.476 --> 11:27.228
Good luck in your fight.

11:31.190 --> 11:32.191
Inosuke.

11:37.238 --> 11:38.280
Let's go.

11:49.125 --> 11:50.501
I'm here to back you up.

11:50.584 --> 11:52.211
I'm a Mizunoto-ranked Slayer,

11:52.294 --> 11:54.130
Tanjiro Kamado.

11:54.213 --> 11:55.548
Mizunoto...

11:56.298 --> 11:57.758
Mizunoto?

11:58.342 --> 12:00.344
Why not Hashira?

12:00.928 --> 12:03.597
No matter how many Mizunoto are here,

12:03.681 --> 12:04.807
it's hopeless.

12:06.434 --> 12:07.560
Inosuke!

12:07.643 --> 12:08.769
You're fussy!

12:08.853 --> 12:10.813
Only planning can do us good.

12:10.896 --> 12:14.275
Your existence doesn't do us any good.

12:14.358 --> 12:17.987
Now tell me what the hell is going on,
you coward!

12:18.070 --> 12:19.738
What's up with this guy?

12:19.822 --> 12:21.907
I'm your senior, you know.

12:22.450 --> 12:25.953
I received a message from the crow.

12:26.620 --> 12:29.081
There were ten of us who came here.

12:32.042 --> 12:34.545
Not long after going into the mountain,

12:34.628 --> 12:35.880
my compatriots...

12:37.423 --> 12:39.425
DESTROY

12:53.731 --> 12:56.108
My compatriots started killing each other.

13:08.204 --> 13:09.246
I...

13:12.666 --> 13:13.626
I...

13:20.049 --> 13:22.009
You took the trouble to fly back.

13:23.385 --> 13:27.139
My slayers should be virtually
annihilated by now.

13:28.432 --> 13:31.227
The Twelve Demon Moons
might be there as well.

13:32.353 --> 13:34.980
Looks like I have to send in the Hashira.

13:40.361 --> 13:41.403
Giyu.

13:43.447 --> 13:44.532
Shinobu.

13:47.284 --> 13:48.327
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

13:50.454 --> 13:53.666
It would be ideal if humans
could get along with demons.

13:53.749 --> 13:55.751
Don't you think so, Mr. Tomioka?

13:56.502 --> 13:58.212
That is utter nonsense

13:58.295 --> 14:00.422
so long as demons don't quit
eating humans.

14:03.050 --> 14:05.511
They already hate me, don't they?

14:07.304 --> 14:11.475
Would an ordinary guy abandon
his own companion on the road?

14:11.559 --> 14:13.644
Shouldn't a companion come to persuade me?

14:14.478 --> 14:16.230
-Had they persuaded me...
-Zenitsu.

14:16.313 --> 14:18.732
-I'd be willing to come along.
-Zenitsu.

14:19.567 --> 14:21.318
But you know those two,

14:21.402 --> 14:24.446
they would take off quickly
towards that scary mountain...

14:25.531 --> 14:27.908
not giving a damn about my feelings
as they abandoned me.

14:35.708 --> 14:38.878
SITTING HERE AND MOPING WON'T HELP.
NOW HURRY AND HELP YOUR COMPANIONS.

14:41.046 --> 14:43.299
That's easy for you to say.

14:43.382 --> 14:46.302
You don't really understand humans.

14:47.386 --> 14:49.972
That hurts!

14:50.055 --> 14:51.682
You're not cute at all!

14:51.765 --> 14:55.644
You're so preachy,
so you're not cute at all!

14:55.728 --> 15:00.232
Even Nezuko is cute as a demon
while you're so fierce for a sparrow!

15:02.693 --> 15:05.821
He took Nezuko away!

15:05.905 --> 15:09.033
Why did he have to take
my treasured Nezuko?

15:09.116 --> 15:11.368
You've gone too far, Tanjiro!

15:11.452 --> 15:13.454
How could you take a girl
to such a dangerous place?

15:13.537 --> 15:14.955
You fool!

15:15.039 --> 15:18.667
Nezuko!

15:27.384 --> 15:29.637
What's that noise?

15:30.262 --> 15:31.305
It's back.

15:32.473 --> 15:34.350
It's this noise.

15:34.433 --> 15:36.060
The minute I heard it,

15:36.143 --> 15:39.063
I turned around and saw
the others hacking each other.

15:40.356 --> 15:41.565
Where is it coming from?

16:24.483 --> 16:26.527
They're all idiots.

16:26.610 --> 16:29.989
They don't know that aiming their blades
at a compatriot is a serious offense.

16:30.072 --> 16:31.156
No, it's not that.

16:31.240 --> 16:32.574
They're moving strangely.

16:32.658 --> 16:34.910
It looks like they're being manipulated.

16:34.994 --> 16:36.036
Good.

16:37.121 --> 16:39.164
Watch as I halve each one of them!

16:39.248 --> 16:40.582
No!

16:40.666 --> 16:41.583
They're alive.

16:41.667 --> 16:43.794
They're still alive inside.

16:43.877 --> 16:47.339
Besides, we can't hack
our own compatriots!

16:49.008 --> 16:53.303
Don't you overrule me all the time!

17:07.651 --> 17:10.946
I can smell a peculiarly sweet scent
on their backs.

17:18.120 --> 17:19.121
There are threads.

17:19.204 --> 17:20.873
They're attached to threads.

17:20.956 --> 17:22.082
Cut the threads!

17:29.840 --> 17:32.426
I noticed them sooner than you.

17:33.427 --> 17:34.720
Where's the bad guy?

17:34.803 --> 17:36.597
Where's the demon pulling the threads?

17:39.308 --> 17:40.309
What is that?

17:40.392 --> 17:42.978
This one's totally pungent,
yet it's brief.

17:46.982 --> 17:48.025
These are...

17:57.785 --> 17:59.036
Spiders!

17:59.119 --> 18:01.455
They're the ones
tying their web threads on people.

18:01.997 --> 18:03.332
So that means...

18:11.840 --> 18:15.177
Come here, my cute little puppets.

18:15.260 --> 18:18.222
Dance like madmen
until your limbs get chopped off.

18:18.847 --> 18:20.766
It's not enough to cut the threads.

18:20.849 --> 18:23.227
The spiders will regenerate them
on our bodies.

18:23.310 --> 18:24.311
So...

18:25.312 --> 18:26.814
It's this pungent odor again.

18:26.897 --> 18:28.232
What the hell is this?

18:28.315 --> 18:30.067
It's blown here by the wind.

18:34.279 --> 18:37.825
Well then, I just have to annihilate
all these spiders.

18:37.908 --> 18:39.076
No, that's impossible.

18:39.159 --> 18:42.037
The spiders are so small
and there are so many of them.

18:42.121 --> 18:44.706
We need to find the demon
who's controlling the spiders.

18:49.628 --> 18:51.130
That's not the way, Inosuke.

18:51.213 --> 18:56.468
Inosuke, if you have the ability
to accurately locate a demon,

18:56.552 --> 18:57.970
help me out.

18:58.053 --> 19:02.641
There was this weird odor blowing this way
and it made my nose numb.

19:03.433 --> 19:05.477
And you, what's your name?

19:05.561 --> 19:06.603
I'm Murata.

19:06.687 --> 19:08.105
Mr. Murata.

19:08.188 --> 19:11.817
You and I will find a way
to save those who are manipulated.

19:11.900 --> 19:12.818
Inosuke--

19:27.624 --> 19:31.295
Don't come here to disturb our family.

19:34.631 --> 19:35.924
He's floating in the air.

19:36.008 --> 19:38.635
No, he's standing on a web thread.

19:39.136 --> 19:40.304
Who's his family?

19:41.138 --> 19:44.516
My mom is going to kill you soon.

19:45.809 --> 19:46.894
"Mom"?

19:58.197 --> 19:59.489
Damn it!

19:59.990 --> 20:02.326
Where do you think you're going?
Come here and fight!

20:03.160 --> 20:04.286
Inosuke.

20:05.120 --> 20:07.289
What the hell is that guy doing here?

20:07.372 --> 20:10.542
I'm afraid that kid is not the one
pulling the threads.

20:10.626 --> 20:12.628
So you should first...

20:12.711 --> 20:15.714
Okay, I get it.

20:16.715 --> 20:19.134
Locate the demon, is that it?

20:19.218 --> 20:20.886
You're one fussy scarface.

20:24.932 --> 20:26.808
Breath of the Beast.

20:26.892 --> 20:30.103
Seventh Fang, Spatial Awareness.

20:58.298 --> 20:59.925
I found it.

21:00.008 --> 21:01.176
It's over there.

21:07.724 --> 21:09.935
I won't let anyone obstruct us.

21:11.436 --> 21:15.107
The five of us have been living
a blissful life.

21:16.358 --> 21:20.153
Our ties will never be broken.

22:52.996 --> 22:55.665
Nezuko, Tanjiro!

22:55.749 --> 22:57.084
Are you there?

22:57.167 --> 22:58.794
CALM DOWN AND LISTEN TO YOUR SURROUNDINGS.

22:58.877 --> 23:02.297
But Nezuko is in danger.
Stop nagging and help me, Chuntaro.

23:02.380 --> 23:03.673
SO YOU MUST CALM DOWN.

23:03.757 --> 23:06.009
HERE'S A LITTLE GOSSIP
FROM THE TAISHO ERA.

23:06.093 --> 23:08.178
MY REAL NAME IS UKOGI.

23:08.261 --> 23:10.514
MY FAVORITE FOOD IS RICE.

23:10.597 --> 23:12.682
ZENITSU NEVER KNEW THIS.
ALL HE GAVE ME WERE BEANS.

23:12.766 --> 23:14.184
What are you grumbling about?

23:14.267 --> 23:15.811
Have some of this to cool down.

23:15.894 --> 23:17.020
IT'S AN UKOGI RICE BALL.

23:17.104 --> 23:18.480
Then I need you to find someone.

23:18.563 --> 23:20.148
Nezuko is in danger.

23:20.899 --> 23:22.692
Nezuko!

23:22.776 --> 23:23.985
THAT'S WHY I CAN'T HATE HIM.

23:24.069 --> 23:27.447
Next, episode 16,
"Letting Someone Else Go First."

23:27.531 --> 23:28.406
TO BE CONTINUED

23:28.490 --> 23:29.574
Subtitle translation by CL Tan
